<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53156" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰπηλ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for a</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπηλος, ζυγόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dinol.
					2
				</span></i>
			 (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπανικόν</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἀργύρωμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					11(2).110
				</span></i>
			 (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>; <i>mercenary</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					4.28
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.48
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -ική</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπηλεία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				223d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1257a18
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπηλικόν, τό</span>, <i>campfollowers, sutlers</i> of an
			army, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>; but also, <i>tax on retailtraders</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1237
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>like a petty trader, knavish, cozening</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. μέτρα φιλεῦσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.229
				</span></i>
			 (Marc. Arg.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕθλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Chr.</u>
					49
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἔχειν</span> to be <i>vamped up
				for sale</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1063
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πράγματα κ. διανέμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.369c
				</span></i>
			; <i>in a mercenary spirit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.216
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Numen.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				14.8
			</span></i>.</div>
